  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Damietta Port II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project is a container terminal with capacity of 3.3 million Twenty-foot equivalent unit (MTEU) located in Damietta Port on the Mediterranean Sea in Egypt (Project). The Project will be carried under a 30-year Concession Agreement granted by the Damietta Port Authority (DPA) under the Ministry of Transport (MoT) . Construction is expected to begin in end of 2023 with initial operations expected to commence in January 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main project-level effect is enhanced access and quality of port services in Egypt through an increase in Port Damietta capacity and operational efficiency with catalyzed economywide effects. Beyond the Project, at the market level, this investment is expected to contribute to enhanced integration through connections to local and new international markets to play a more prominent role in Egypts trade while expanding transshipment through connecting additional shipping lines. This will further support the integration and economic development of the east-Mediterranean region to help position Egypt as a global hub for logistics and trade.</narrative>
  </description>
